- [Scar Standard]: Scars can exhibit a range of attributes influenced by their underlying causes, encompassing inflammatory and reactive processes to malignancies and dermatosis conditions. Examination of scars should focus on well-defined borders, stable surface quality, and the absence of ulcers, crusts, atrophy, or lichenification. Irregular shapes, varying degrees of redness, pigmentation, vascular changes, and structural patterns may also be observed. Internal architectural patterns like pigment networks, globules, or regression structures are typically absent. When analyzing scars using dermoscopy, it is crucial to consider these core visual features for accurate diagnoses and differentiation among various scar types.
